                                "sense_id": "cb31507d-1061-391c-8d03-93b3aa4c4702",
                                "text": "When the rains descend and the floods come the Ouse swells, muddens, and overspreads the meadows in a methodical manner, doing its overflowing with dismal thoroughness, but conducting itself with persistent respectability, under circumstances which would warrant any other river in roaring and trampling over all that lay in its way."
